- [x] Fix MIPS o32 aggregate-return ABI handling in imported PCC.
  - No-argument struct/union-return calls now still run through target
    `funcode()` so the hidden result pointer is emitted.
  - Struct/union return temporaries now allocate a full stack object via
    `cstknode()` instead of a single temp word.
  - Callee parameter stack offsets are shifted by one o32 slot after the hidden
    `$a0` result pointer.
  - This fixed `c99/func003` and `jira/PCC-138`; it also exposed the separate
    `jira/PCC-85` stack alignment failure fixed below.
- [x] Fix MIPS o32 stack alignment for stack-passed call arguments.
  - `lastcall()` now computes the real `FUNARG` push size after target
    lowering and emits a pre-argument pad when the pushed stack arguments would
    leave `$sp` only 4-byte aligned.
  - This keeps the ABI position of the first stack argument intact while
    preserving the existing rounded post-call cleanup.
  - This fixed `jira/PCC-85`, which was faulting in `_doprnt` at
    `sdc1 $f26,504(sp)` because `$sp` reached GCC-built libc misaligned.
- [x] Fix MIPS memory integer-to-double conversion.
  - `SOREG TWORD -> double/long double` conversion now loads the 32-bit
    integer word into an FPU register with `l.s` before `cvt.d.w`.
  - The old `l.d` form required 8-byte alignment and read past the integer
    slot.
  - This fixed `jira/PCC-236`.
- [x] Fix MIPS big-endian sub-word bitfield reads and padding clears.
  - `rmfldops()` now computes big-endian bit offsets from the actual storage
    unit type (`char`, `short`, `int`, or `long long`) instead of the promoted
    result type.
  - Automatic aggregate initialization now clears sub-byte padding spans with
    byte-sized bitfield stores, avoiding unaligned word RMW sequences.
  - This fixed `jira/PCC-462`; it changed the failure from an unaligned memory
    fault, through a diagnostic return code of 4, to a clean Malta pass.
